  {"op": "index", "title": "P5-2 landform look: Valley, Hilltop, Terraces, Lakeshore, Gorge", "intro": "Produced by tools/render_jobs/jobs/landform_look.json at 1920x1080. New 150 ft maps opened through NewMap.create (probes/landform.gd new), each saved as _p5_<kind>_<biome>_<seed>. Valley (P5-1, retuned in P5-2 to 3.5 m deep with the rim at 0.6 of the half extent): temperate forest seeds 1234 (dry, a wash), 2 (a river), 3 (a river with a ford) and 4 (a river with a tributary), rocky badlands 1234. Hilltop: forest 7 (a crown, a spring from its foot with a fall, stones) and 12 (no crown, a second hill, dry), alpine meadow 7. Terraces: forest 3 (three tiers, a river with two falls, a plank bridge) and 9 (two tiers, dry), boreal taiga 3. Lakeshore: forest 5 (an islet, a feeding stream with stones) and 2 (the lake alone), wetland riparian 5. Gorge: forest 7 (two tiers, a stream, an arch) and 1 (one tier, two bends, a dry wash), rocky badlands 7. Per level: home with the grid, home with the water hidden (wet draws), zoom 8 on the stage and zoom 8 on the crossing, the water or the floor. Then the Valley's seed 3 is played and a token dropped on its ford. Judge from the home camera: does each landform read as a place (a hill with a rock-lipped crown, tiers stepping down with their faces, a lake with its shore, a ravine with walls), does the dry draw stand on its own, is the stage open and dry, do the water and the crossing sit right. Reports (the recipe's draw per level) are in log.txt (landform.gd new / report)."},
